{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209070-some-storytelling-advice","id":1209070,"title":"Some Storytelling Advice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-19T17:33:42-07:00","id":1209070,"title":"Some Storytelling Advice","content":"Alright, so I've mused about this elsewhere but I figured long form thinking it out and asking for help would be best on the forum. <br /> So, in my current Gothic Horror Mystery Game, one of the three big bads is an old and isolated sorcerer who has made contact with entities from the Upper Ocean(the region of the stars, that shields creation from the full brunt of the sun). He's engaged in research of prior worshipers of the Lovecraftian creatures that lurk in that strange sea, and has been conducting experiments on fusing these creatures with human beings to create an elevated form of life (at request of the local king, who wants an edge over a local rival dragonblooded nation), including himself. The eventual plan, plot wise, is for him to introduce more widespread mutation and terror in the capital itself.<br /> I've been considering whether this scope is something that should be kept as a unique entity--because of his contact with powerful and ancient spirits having warped him in someway, he's been turned into a stranger thing, a complete unknown or unique being in Exalted--or if he should be a Solar (the party is currently an Abyssal, 2 exigents, a lunar and a dragonblooded) to play off his nature as a fundamentally human pursuit of power and insight. <br /> Does anyone have any thoughts?<br /> <br /> For perspective, the other big bads are a circle of Lunar revolutionaires, and an infernal pirate crew plotting a coup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T18:51:49-07:00","id":1209085,"title":"","content":"Keep him unique? I mean, I think part of the fundamental to &quot;horror mystery&quot; is <b>not knowing</b> - and <b>never knowing. </b><br /> <br /> You, the ST, can know what he is..... but that's irrelevant to the players, unless they specifically have some kind of magic to tell them the difference between a Solar &amp; a (unique entity).<br /> <br /> Just my 2 pesos.<br /> <br /> Or is there another question I'm missing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T18:54:04-07:00","id":1209086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209070-some-storytelling-advice?p=1209085#post1209085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep him unique? I mean, I think part of the fundamental to &quot;horror mystery&quot; is <b>not knowing</b> - and <b>never knowing. </b><br /> <br /> You, the ST, can know what he is..... but that's irrelevant to the players, unless they specifically have some kind of magic to tell them the difference between a Solar &amp; a (unique entity).<br /> <br /> Just my 2 pesos.<br /> <br /> Or is there another question I'm missing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nah, that was the question.<br /> <br /> As for the players knowing...well, if he Bonfires, they'll kinda know :P<br /> <br /> Him being a solar would be a reveal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?