in choosing his peeps, so I guess the question to you is if you see the UCS as choosing this broheim or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T19:51:32-07:00","id":1209101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209070-some-storytelling-advice?p=1209088#post1209088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Epee, if this is 3E remember the UCS now has a much more active role in choosing his peeps, so I guess the question to you is if you see the UCS as choosing this broheim or not?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hm. My thought was his momnt of exaltation was the creation of a portal to the Upper Sea. Single minded obsession might be outside the purview of the UCS's favored traits, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T00:00:33-07:00","id":1209130,"title":"","content":"I'd avoid making him a Solar. You have a really great start at a &quot;Steal Fire From the Gods&quot; plot going on here, and this guy is definitely leaping off the slippery slope into things Man Was Not Meant To Know. He has gone from Uyi Schor, Mortal Sorcerer to <b>Yischo, </b><b>Divine Beast of the Sky Sea</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T17:03:36-07:00","id":1209457,"title":"","content":"I'd make him a Solar. I don't think making him Not A Solar is a bad idea either, but I notice a distinct lack of Solars mentioned in your game, most notably in the PC group. With no Solar Heroes, this is a great chance to make a Solar Villain whose reveal might be a genuine surprise, when they push him to his limit and he becomes a blasphemous flailing tentacle monster aflame with Ultimate Power. Your Abyssals will hate him extra-hard if/when he starts hypocritically rebuking them as CoD, especially if he threatens them with anything Holy. Do they have any respect for the UCS? Because this guy makes a complete and utter mockery of His divine authority.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, how does your table feel about Solars, like, in general? I've been drilling it into my players that Solars are the very definition of Power for like 10 years but almost never make a Solar NPC, so when I do they shit their pants a little because they know it potentially means the biggest threat possible. But that's a veteran Exalted group. Newer players might not have a long-time respect for Solars as more than the standard PC choice. If that's closer to your group, then maybe don't make it a Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","user":"JTroy","date":". 04-20-2018, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T05:15:55-07:00","id":1209583,"title":"","content":"<b>re: Solars and Holy</b><br /> <br /> The &quot;hypocrisy&quot; of a malevolent Solar using Holy vs an Abyssal (who one presumes isn't trying to murder everything) can be a good idea. It hammers home that Holy <b>isn't</b> &quot;Lawful Good&quot; and is instead more like &quot;my daddy's the mayor - the cops are arresting you, not me&quot;. <b>And truth be told</b>, while I avoid Solars, they <b>do</b> make fantastic demonologists (precisely because of Holy - it <b>isn't</b> just combat - there were Holy tagged social charms, meaning a Solar has more mental/emotional sway over demons than others).<br /> <br /> Hell, if you wanted to be &quot;cruel&quot; about it, play up to Theion-styled &quot;big ball of glorious light flame&quot; when Holy is used. It's less &quot;I'm brow-beating you into subservience&quot; and more &quot;I remind you guys a lot of what you once were...&quot;<br /> <br /> re: Bonfires<br /> <br /> Irrelevant! You don't need to be a Twilight to be a sorceror or dabble with horrors. A Night Caste could suppress their anima over and over.<br /> <br /> <b>Or</b> introduce a hearthstone or item to hide it. There some Fire-themed Hearthstones that gave you a faux Fire-Aspect anima banner (great for masquerading along). <b>By extension</b>, I'm not saying &quot;pretend to be a Fire-Aspect&quot; but merely &quot;don't feel like you NEED to reveal your anima banner&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T06:29:56-07:00","id":1209597,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar848_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"848\" data-vbnamecard=\"848\">JTroy</a> the players are fairly aware of how dangerous a solar can be, mostly by having played a few games as them and caused no small amount of havoc on their own. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> the response to realizing the strange old man they are suspicious of is actually a solar would hopefully provoke the reaction your describing.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23843_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23843\" data-vbnamecard=\"23843\">Salagimsim</a> and you make a good point regarding holy, which would also apply to one of the Exigents. As for Bonfires, his bonfire moment would be in a moment of triumphant \u201cYou fools cannot comprehend the trouble your in\u201d moment.<br /> Incidentally he is a twilight, mainly because his role is a scholar (so Lore Occutl Medicine And Buer are caste abilities if he has them)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8830_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8830\" data-vbnamecard=\"8830\">Sorcerous Overlord</a> those are hella names and I\u2019m using at least the second one(the characters mortal name has already been revealed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":11835,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","user":"Epee102","date":".  god tags are hard on mobile. 04-21-2018, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T07:30:48-07:00","id":1209618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209070-some-storytelling-advice#post1209070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been considering whether this scope is something that should be kept as a unique entity--because of his contact with powerful and ancient spirits having warped him in someway, he's been turned into a stranger thing, a complete unknown or unique being in Exalted--or if he should be a Solar (the party is currently an Abyssal, 2 exigents, a lunar and a dragonblooded) to play off his nature as a fundamentally human pursuit of power and insight.<br /> Does anyone have any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd go with unique entity on the very shallow basis that the Solar aesthetics and the Lovecraftian one don't really mesh well (<a href=\"https://youtu.be/XlyC6OoXTds\" target=\"_blank\">exceptions nonwithstanding</a>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T07:41:24-07:00","id":1209620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209070-some-storytelling-advice?p=1209583#post1209583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>re: Solars and Holy</b><br /> <br /> The &amp;quot;hypocrisy&amp;quot; of a malevolent Solar using Holy vs an Abyssal (who one presumes isn't trying to murder everything) can be a good idea. It hammers home that Holy <b>isn't</b> &amp;quot;Lawful Good&amp;quot; and is instead more like &amp;quot;my daddy's the mayor - the cops are arresting you, not me&amp;quot;. <b>And truth be told</b>, while I avoid Solars, they <b>do</b> make fantastic demonologists (precisely because of Holy - it <b>isn't</b> just combat - there were Holy tagged social charms, meaning a Solar has more mental/emotional sway over demons than others).<br /> <br /> Hell, if you wanted to be &amp;quot;cruel&amp;quot; about it, play up to Theion-styled &amp;quot;big ball of glorious light flame&amp;quot; when Holy is used. It's less &amp;quot;I'm brow-beating you into subservience&amp;quot; and more &amp;quot;I remind you guys a lot of what you once were...&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> re: Bonfires<br /> <br /> Irrelevant! You don't need to be a Twilight to be a sorceror or dabble with horrors. A Night Caste could suppress their anima over and over.<br /> <br /> <b>Or</b> introduce a hearthstone or item to hide it. There some Fire-themed Hearthstones that gave you a faux Fire-Aspect anima banner (great for masquerading along). <b>By extension</b>, I'm not saying &amp;quot;pretend to be a Fire-Aspect&amp;quot; but merely &amp;quot;don't feel like you NEED to reveal your anima banner&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It\u2019s less that than that in 3E Sol Invictus actively CHOOSES who exalts. Exaltation is no longer an autonomous programmed thing. So it\u2019s not about him using \u201choly\u201d as much as Sol going \u201cyeah, I totally want someone being my chosen working with lovecraftian entities\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T11:26:24-07:00","id":1209704,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209070-some-storytelling-advice?p=1209620#post1209620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s less that than that in 3E Sol Invictus actively CHOOSES who exalts. Exaltation is no longer an autonomous programmed thing. So it\u2019s not about him using \u201choly\u201d as much as Sol going \u201cyeah, I totally want someone being my chosen working with lovecraftian entities\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div></div> Ah, the change in Editions, lol.<br /> <br /> The point remains (somewhat). In Glories of the Most High - Sol - one of the problems it brings up is that Sol Invictus is of such <b>extreme Virtue</b>, that Virtues naturally contradict one another. <b>Therefore</b>, he has to suppress them.<br /> <br /> For example, Compassion <i>compels</i> him to save the world - but he suppresses that for a scene to go hide in the Jade Pleasure Dome. Awesome, he's no longer faced with suffering, so he doesn't have to suppress Compassion - <b>but now</b> Temperance is likely suppressed by virtue to his own addiction to the Games of Divinity. Etc, etc, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> IE, Sol isn't always consistent.<br /> <br /> Plus the Roll of Glorious Divinity <b>has an ambassador to Maleas/YuShan</b> god who has proven loyal for a few centuries.<br /> <br /> Plus - in 3E, Twilights <i>explicitly</i> have that new ability to bind a demon or elemental as a Familiar. Hardly &quot;Sol disapproves&quot;, no?<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Ergo</b><ul><li>Perhaps the Twilight was chosen for legit occult expertise? <b>Only after (X) event later </b>did one obsession follow another and they eventually went Lovecraftean.</li> <li>Not all horrors are inhuman. Going to 2E, Malfeas' charms imply a permanent PTSD-nightmare with awareness charms &quot;only good enough&quot; to let you know a <i>possible</i> threat is nearby. Adorjan's compassion is crazy. Theion did conviction. The Ebon Dragon shuns Virtue as She Who Lives In Her Name takes them to impersonal extremes.<ul><li>Malfeas and Cearr are a great example - the signature Slayer was literally Chosen after a battlefield where his whole tribe was exterminated between 2 larger armies and a monster. PTSD really fits. The day he gets &quot;Nightmare Fugue Vigilance&quot;, he'll never sleep - but also gets permanent-nightmares as he's awake.</li> <li>Adorjan has another example in her compassion charms - she can literally make herself &quot;love' you (and in that, become better at teaching, helping or hurting you). The Twilight could be a victim who earned her unfortunate affections and was warped thereafter.</li> </ul></li> </ul>Etc, etc.<br /> <br /> My mention of Holy for Demonology is <b>less </b>&quot;Sol picked a Yozi cultists and gave him power&quot; and <b>more </b>&quot;Sol picked (X) hero who - upon realizing they could brow-beat demons with ease - ended up among them more often&quot;. I've built a few &quot;pro-Demon&quot; Exalts (Eclipses, Night, etc) - not loyal to the Yozis or anything - but merely prone to working with demons more often (since my charms guaranteed obedience). They stayed &quot;on the good side&quot; but had Adorjan showed up with charm-set, I wouldn't be surprised if they were wooed over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T13:55:02-07:00","id":1209770,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23843_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23843\" data-vbnamecard=\"23843\">Salagimsim</a> as to virtues, and the applicablity of Glories RE: 3e. Virtues are not discrete entities nor are they a system in game (no temperance, courage, etc as stats). <br /> <br /> Additionally, Devs typically have rolled back most if not all 2e material to 1e (broadly speaking). A better reference from their perspective is games of divinity but only to a point.<br /> <br /> My point was more given the nature of how Epee had pitched the WHEN of a potential exaltation, that it might not be appropriate, as sol would know what exactly he was working toward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T15:16:35-07:00","id":1209786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209070-some-storytelling-advice?p=1209770#post1209770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23843_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23843\" data-vbnamecard=\"23843\">Salagimsim</a> as to virtues, and the applicablity of Glories RE: 3e. Virtues are not discrete entities nor are they a system in game (no temperance, courage, etc as stats).<br /> <br /> Additionally, Devs typically have rolled back most if not all 2e material to 1e (broadly speaking). A better reference from their perspective is games of divinity but only to a point.<br /> <br /> My point was more given the nature of how Epee had pitched the WHEN of a potential exaltation, that it might not be appropriate, as sol would know what exactly he was working toward.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of exaltation being the creation of a portal to a previously untapped realm? To be clear &quot;Become a starspawn&quot; was his goal after exploring it a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T15:25:41-07:00","id":1209790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209070-some-storytelling-advice?p=1209786#post1209786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The point of exaltation being the creation of a portal to a previously untapped realm? To be clear &amp;quot;Become a starspawn&amp;quot; was his goal after exploring it a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I guess the question is would that be a thing Sol would reward? Given his more active role in choosing, does that act align with what he views as a \u201cyeah I totally want this guy to be my champion\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}